<entry dateCreated="2005-06-23T16:08:17Z" dateModified="2026-09-28T19:39:52Z" id="mu-4_6283da64-0a0e-4aad-adca-cb7aff6a4e13" guid="6283da64-0a0e-4aad-adca-cb7aff6a4e13" order="4">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="seh"><text>mu-</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>mw-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [AEI]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>m'-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/_[LabAsp]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>m-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [Lab]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>n'-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [nonlabialaspirated]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>n-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [C]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>m'-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/_[LabAsp]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>m-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [Lab]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>n-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ [C]"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<sense id="b452249d-5017-4d97-9f0d-447aed630bf3">
<grammatical-info value="Verbo">
<trait name="type" value="inflAffix"/>
<trait name="Verbo-slot" value="obj"/><trait name="Verbo-slot" value="sbj"/></grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>2P</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="pt"><text>2P</text></gloss>
<definition>
<form lang="en"><text>second person plural, "you"</text></form>
<form lang="pt"><text>segunda pessoa plural, "vocês"</text></form>
</definition>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>Question: Are there any examples of mw/ _ [V]? Question: 0 / _ [nasal] | how to handle nullsdefine bilabial and stops; May require a mcc +/ [tense] ... _ to prevent some ambiguities; Question: what is it before a vowel?; a m / _ [labial] / _ [OU] | eg. kumpa kumona kumolota kumulaya; a n / _ [C] | eg. kunsowera</text></form>
</note>
<note type="phonology">
<form lang="en"><text>alt: <span lang="seh">mw / _ [V] |fails for PART: mbamuapfunzisa; mu / _ [C]; mu +/ PART..._; mu +/ _ {monosyllabic} | eg. munthu; mw / _ [V] | eg. mwana mwimbi *mwonsense; m' / _ [labialaspirated] | eg. m'bale; m / _ [labial] | eg. mpfunzisi; n' / _ [nonlabialaspirated] | eg. n'th??; n / _ [C] | eg. nkolakazi nzungu nrimi; mu; m' / _ [labialaspirated]; m / _ [labial] |eg pi-da-m-menye ka-m-bhoma; n' / _ [nonlabialaspirated] |eg. ka-n'-khucha; n / _ [C] |eg ka-n-tema (cortar); mu / _ [V] |eg pi-da-mu-ona; mu |eg amulamusa</span></text></form>
</note>
<note type="source">
<form lang="en"><text>Schadeberg 2.1.3.8</text></form>
</note>
<field type="Parsing Note">
<form lang="en"><text>This is used as a nominalizer as well kutumwa &gt; m'tumwa/m'tumwi; Seem that there are times that the m' rule does not apply. Why?</text></form>
</field>
</sense>
</entry>

